values
  ('agent_tool:check_workforce_registry', 'Real departments/roles/capabilities org model', 'The real, static, always-accurate departments (25), specialist roles (85), and Hermes mission-engine capability implementation statuses (30 keys, each explicitly AVAILABLE/PLANNED/NOT_CONFIGURED/UNAVAILABLE -- never defaulted) modeled in packages/workforce-core. A different axis from this table itself: this row''s tool answers "does the mission engine model X as implemented at all", not "can a human reach X via WhatsApp right now". Zero-cost, zero-risk -- reads nothing from a database or network, so it can never be stale relative to deployed code. Live-verified this pass: 25 departments, 85 roles, capability status counts confirmed against the real unmocked package.', 'ecosystem', 'workforce org-model read', 'check_workforce_registry', 'packages/workforce-core (departments/roles/capabilities registries)', 'Engineering', null, 'agent:read:capabilities', 'read', 'platform_only', 'free', 'read', 'none (read-only, in-memory static data)', 'REAL_EXPOSED', 'AVAILABLE in this registry describes implementation, not live autonomous execution -- hermesMode is disabled in production (see engine:hermes_missions), so missions do not currently run unattended even for AVAILABLE capabilities.', null, now(), 'claude_session_2026-09-02');
